@name Explainer 8: Cooke triplet re-optimised for f/2
# Explainer #8: the Cooke triplet of lenses/cooke-triplet.lens re-optimised
# for f/2: same glasses (N-SK16 / F2 / N-SK16), same structure, iris behind
# the middle element.
# Role: three thin lenses have no freedoms left for f/2; higher-order
# aberrations take over.
# Design: all six curvatures, the three glass thicknesses and the air gaps
# (stop position included) vary (EFL 50 mm), minimising the white-light RMS
# spot at 0, 0.5, 0.7 and 1.0 of the field, object at 2.5 m;
# vignetting towards the corner up to half the light.
#
# Generated by `lens-render optimize lenses/explainer/08-triplet-f2.toml`.
# RMS spot (F, e, C) at f/2, object at 2.5 m, by image height
# (fraction of 21.63 mm): 0: 36.1, 0.5: 39.7, 0.7: 54.3, 1: 33.6 µm. Units: mm.
#
# radius      thickness   material       semi-diameter
